From 50862278183ad39c6907a5649c0283817451d4e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 18:17:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(grounding): P1 fail-closed gate.read_first blocks unread
 claims

Register rail.grounding (master, unlocked, default-ON) + gate.read_first +
gate.cite in DEFAULT_GRAPH following the gate.issue_verify shape (phase-less,
unlocked, default-ON, toggled via workflow.gates). forge recap/show append a
context.loaded kernel event (pure append via insertKernelEvent, gate-events
pattern) with {actor, session, cmd, budget}. forge claim <id> HARD-BLOCKS
(exit 6) when the issue exists but has no fresh context.loaded event this
session/24h-window; the block message is the exact remedy `forge recap <id>
first`, so the cheapest path through the gate is the correct behavior.

The gate is inert for issues absent from the consulted kernel (a real claim on
a non-existent issue fails on its own) and fail-open on kernel-unavailable, so
existing claim tests are unaffected. gate.cite is registered but its scanner is
P3. Session Tier-1 (harness id) is honored when present; the 24h window is the
agnostic floor. rail.grounding / gate.read_first disabled -> allow, logged.

Adversarial tests first (red): claim-without-recap blocks; recap-then-claim
passes; both toggles off -> allow; context.loaded append-only + idempotent per
window + survives across processes.

Refs e037a559-d3a9-4bfa-8ac2-346e61f48999 (epic 6ef96e92-848e-4360-9c81-456b6b151e51).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
